  \item
    \(8.15\)
  \item
    \(180.17\)
  \end{enumerate}

  \textbf{Solution}\\
  Para o cálculo da variância precisamos, antes, calcular os valores de
  \(E(Y)\) e \(E(Y^2)\): \[\begin{aligned}
  E(Y) &= \sum_{i=1}^5 y_i~P(Y=y_i) \\
  & = 0 \times 0.26+
  5 \times 0.28+10 \times 0.17+
  15 \times 0.15+20 \times 0.14 = 8.15,
  \end{aligned}\] \[\begin{aligned}
  E(Y^2) &= \sum_{i=1}^5 {y_i}^2~P(Y=y_i) \\
  & = 0 \times 0.26+
  25 \times 0.28+100 \times 0.17+
  225 \times 0.15+400 \times 0.14 \\
  & =113.75.
  \end{aligned}\] De modo que
  \(V(Y) = E(Y^2) - \left\{E(Y)\right\}^2 = 47.33\).

